WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.001
Three services keep their
own device inventory,

2
00:00:03.001 --> 00:00:05.362
and they disagree in predictable ways.

3
00:00:05.362 --> 00:00:09.144
Intune's managed devices drift
when devices stop checking in,

4
00:00:09.144 --> 00:00:10.849
and cleanup rules hide them.

5
00:00:10.849 --> 00:00:14.482
Entra ID accumulates stale
objects from reimaging,

6
00:00:14.482 --> 00:00:18.113
broken hybrid trust, or
devices that never enrolled.

7
00:00:18.113 --> 00:00:23.400
Defender has devices onboarded but not
enrolled, or enrolled but never onboarded.

8
00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:27.112
The program reconciles them
weekly on the Entra device ID.

9
00:00:27.112 --> 00:00:30.873
Every enrolled device must have
an Entra object with its tier,

10
00:00:30.873 --> 00:00:35.001
role and environment attributes
set, and a healthy Defender sensor.

11
00:00:35.001 --> 00:00:39.725
Every Entra object for a corporate Windows
device must have an Intune enrollment.

12
00:00:39.725 --> 00:00:44.266
A device missing from any one is a
finding, and the same comparison is the

13
00:00:44.266 --> 00:00:49.037
evidence for CM-8's requirement of a
complete inventory with no duplicates.

14
00:00:49.037 --> 00:00:50.726
Stale records need care.

15
00:00:50.726 --> 00:00:55.617
Intune cleanup rules hide devices after
thirty to two hundred seventy days,

16
00:00:55.617 --> 00:00:58.800
per platform; the program
uses ninety for Windows.

17
00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:03.888
They don't wipe or retire anything,
and hidden devices stay in Entra ID.

18
00:01:03.888 --> 00:01:07.622
Entra's last sign-in timestamp
isn't updated on every sign-in,

19
00:01:07.622 --> 00:01:11.508
so Microsoft advises not treating
anything newer than about

20
00:01:11.508 --> 00:01:15.013
twenty-one days as stale, and
disabling before deleting.

21
00:01:15.013 --> 00:01:19.488
Hybrid devices are removed in Active
Directory, and the change syncs.

22
00:01:19.488 --> 00:01:21.434
Retirement follows a fixed order,

23
00:01:21.434 --> 00:01:24.562
because the order decides
what can still be recovered.

24
00:01:24.562 --> 00:01:29.099
Record first: export the BitLocker
keys and the LAPS password.

25
00:01:29.099 --> 00:01:32.913
Retiring or deleting the Intune
object of an Entra-joined

26
00:01:32.913 --> 00:01:36.488
BitLocker device suspends
BitLocker, so back up first.

27
00:01:36.488 --> 00:01:39.794
Then act on the device:
wipe a corporate device,

28
00:01:39.794 --> 00:01:43.362
retire a personal one;
actions run at next check-in.

29
00:01:43.362 --> 00:01:46.275
Deregister from Autopilot
if it's leaving for good.

30
00:01:46.275 --> 00:01:48.087
Delete the Intune record.

31
00:01:48.087 --> 00:01:51.608
And delete the Entra object
last, after a disable period,

32
00:01:51.608 --> 00:01:54.363
because that permanently deletes its keys.

33
00:01:54.363 --> 00:01:56.836
Plan mass refreshes in daily batches:

34
00:01:56.836 --> 00:02:01.300
the tenant limit is a thousand
retires and a thousand deletes a day.
